# Database credentials, read by docker compose. Only the root .env is ignored:
# frontend/.env holds nothing but a localhost URL and a feature flag, so it is
# committed on purpose to keep the project runnable straight after a clone.
/.env
!/.env.example

# Local overrides of appsettings.json. The committed appsettings.json holds no
# secrets at all: the connection string and the JWT key come from User Secrets
# in development and from environment variables in production (see README.md).
MedGid.API/appsettings.Local.json
